<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta http-equiv="refresh" content="10" />
    <title>Back in a moment</title>
    <!--
      The page Caddy shows for this app when it is down, restarting or being updated (502, 503, 504). A promotion copies it to
      the platform; an app without one gets the platform's plain page. It is served under a policy that allows inline CSS and
      nothing else: no script, no external file, no remote image (images as data: URLs). Make it the app's own: a CSS
      animation, the app's colours. The meta refresh retries every 10 seconds. docs/login-for-apps.md, "The entrance".
    -->
    <style>
      :root { color-scheme: light dark; }
      body { margin: 0; min-height: 100vh; display: grid; place-items: center; font: 16px/1.5 system-ui, sans-serif; background: Canvas; color: CanvasText; text-align: center; }
      main { padding: 24px; max-width: 28rem; }
      h1 { font-size: 1.5rem; margin: 0 0 0.5rem; }
      p { margin: 0; opacity: 0.7; }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <h1>{{name}}</h1>
      <p>Back in a moment. This page tries again by itself.</p>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
